1
00:00:04,754 --> 00:00:07,119
The Lives of the Prophets; Part 1

2
00:00:07,651 --> 00:00:11,389
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:20,128
Syedina Yaqub عليه السّلام requested his sons; to go look for Yusuf(يوسُف) and his brother Binyamin(بنيامين);

4
00:00:23,123 --> 00:00:25,758
 Because he never lost hope in Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

5
00:00:27,433 --> 00:00:37,250
And the next year they went to Egypt to receive the ration.

6
00:00:40,059 --> 00:00:46,886
And they carried with them their merchandise that was sent back with them from the year before.

7
00:00:47,704 --> 00:00:55,160
They went to SadyinaYusuf عليه السّلام and they met with him and they said;

8
00:00:55,256 --> 00:01:31,465
فَلَمَّا دَخَلُوا عَلَيْهِ قَالُوا يَا أَيُّهَا الْعَزِيزُ مَسَّنَا وَأَهْلَنَا الضُّرُّ وَجِئْنَا بِبِضَاعَةٍ مُزْجَاةٍ فَأَوْفِ لَنَا الْكَيْلَ وَتَصَدَّقْ عَلَيْنَا

9
00:01:34,899 --> 00:01:45,225
إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَجْزِي الْمُتَصَدِّقِينَ۝

10
00:01:45,448 --> 00:01:47,778
Then when they entered unto him, they said;

11
00:01:47,881 --> 00:01:53,638
Oh ruler of the land; A hard time has hit us and our family, difficult moments.

12
00:01:54,225 --> 00:02:01,113
It was famine and it was continuing from year to year, and it's becoming more difficult throughout time;

13
00:02:01,415 --> 00:02:05,415
and things were becoming more constrained and more severe.

14
00:02:06,772 --> 00:02:12,197
So they went to SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) and they were begging him.

15
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:14,609
مَسَّنَا وَأَهْلَنَا الضُّرُّ

16
00:02:15,165 --> 00:02:19,451
Harm has befalled us with our families.

17
00:02:20,094 --> 00:02:22,110
وَجِئْنَا بِبِضَاعَةٍ مُزْجَاةٍ

18
00:02:22,412 --> 00:02:25,840
And we have came with poor capital.

19
00:02:26,067 --> 00:02:33,466
Bidhaa Muzjaa(بِبِضَاعَةٍ مُزْجَاةٍ) means some merchandise that is not very good quality.

20
00:02:35,387 --> 00:02:37,331
Something that is not worth a lot.

21
00:02:38,276 --> 00:02:39,818
So they're telling Al-Aziz(ألعزيز);

22
00:02:40,096 --> 00:02:43,770
Al-Aziz(ألعزيز) which is SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) and that's the name of this position.

23
00:02:43,826 --> 00:02:47,331
Al-Aziz(ألعزيز) and the word Al-Aziz(ألعزيز) itself means; the honored.

24
00:02:49,219 --> 00:02:52,768
And they're telling him; really we want you to help us

25
00:02:52,840 --> 00:03:00,263
because this merchandise that we brought with us is not worth a lot; It's not even worth presenting to you;

26
00:03:00,406 --> 00:03:04,588
so they're apologizing before they even present it because they know that it's worthless.

27
00:03:04,977 --> 00:03:08,491
وَجِئْنَا بِبِضَاعَةٍ مُزْجَاةٍ فَأَوْفِ لَنَا الْكَيْلَ

28
00:03:08,785 --> 00:03:10,364
So pay us full measure.

29
00:03:11,071 --> 00:03:12,134
And then they said;

30
00:03:12,515 --> 00:03:16,544
وَتَصَدَّقْ عَلَيْنَا

31
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:19,234
And be charitable to us.

32
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:21,747
They're asking for Sadaqah(صدقة).

33
00:03:22,175 --> 00:03:24,175
They're asking for charity.

34
00:03:26,382 --> 00:03:30,167
When SadyinaYusuf عليه السّلام saw his brothers begging;

35
00:03:31,167 --> 00:03:34,103
When he saw that they reached to the level of begging;

36
00:03:34,619 --> 00:03:39,960
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله) look at this; These brothers who made the conspiracy to get rid of him and kill him.

37
00:03:40,662 --> 00:03:45,804
So they reached to the level of weakness where they are begging their brother whom they don't know.

38
00:03:46,970 --> 00:03:48,748
And they're telling him; Give us charity.

39
00:03:50,962 --> 00:03:51,453
And they said;

40
00:03:51,483 --> 00:03:53,164
إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَجْزِي الْمُتَصَدِّقِينَ۝

41
00:03:53,281 --> 00:03:55,648
Truly Allah does reward charitable.

42
00:03:56,807 --> 00:04:01,396
At that point, when Yusuf(يوسُف) saw his brothers begging, he didn't want it to go any further.

43
00:04:01,984 --> 00:04:04,586
He didn't want them to go under that level.

44
00:04:04,689 --> 00:04:10,721
I mean, that's it when you beg, that's the lowest it could get and the weakest.

45
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:14,173
And he did not want to see his brothers in that position.

46
00:04:14,753 --> 00:04:19,389
Even though they harmed him and they caused them all of this trouble and they throw him in the well.

47
00:04:19,612 --> 00:04:22,453
And they tried to kill him and he's their brother.

48
00:04:23,184 --> 00:04:28,160
But I didn't want to see them in that position of beggars.

49
00:04:28,882 --> 00:04:29,771
So he said;

50
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:50,022
قَالَ هَلْ عَلِمْتُم مَّا فَعَلْتُم بِيُوسُفَ وَأَخِيهِ إِذْ أَنتُمْ جَاهِلُونَ۝

51
00:04:50,314 --> 00:04:55,665
He said; Do you know; What you have done to Yusuf(يوسُف) and his brother.

52
00:04:56,395 --> 00:04:57,960
إِذْ أَنتُمْ جَاهِلُونَ۝

53
00:04:58,222 --> 00:04:59,675
When you were ignorant.

54
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:05,754
Do you know what you have done to Yusuf(يوسُف) and his brother.?

55
00:05:06,278 --> 00:05:09,135
Who can say this except Yusuf(يوسُف) himself?

56
00:05:11,016 --> 00:05:13,062
Who knows about Yusuf(يوسُف).

57
00:05:13,151 --> 00:05:15,102
How Al-Aziz(ألعزيز) know about that?

58
00:05:16,226 --> 00:05:21,336
So immediately when he said that they realize that they're speaking to Yusuf(يوسُف).

59
00:05:23,431 --> 00:05:26,281
When he asked them, What have you done with Yusuf(يوسُف) and his brother?

60
00:05:26,606 --> 00:05:30,832
They knew that the man who's standing in front of them is Yusuf عليه السّلام.

61
00:05:31,141 --> 00:05:31,765
They said;

62
00:05:31,825 --> 00:05:55,833
قَالُوا أَإِنَّكَ لَأَنْتَ يُوسُفُ ۖ قَالَ أَنَا يُوسُفُ وَهَٰذَا أَخِي ۖ قَدْ مَنَّ اللَّهُ عَلَيْنَا ۖ

63
00:05:56,204 --> 00:05:58,752
They said; Are you indeed Yusuf(يوسُف),

64
00:05:59,442 --> 00:06:02,462
قَالَ أَنَا يُوسُفُ وَهَٰذَا أَخِي

65
00:06:02,661 --> 00:06:04,661
I am Yusuf(يوسُف) and this is my brother.

66
00:06:04,804 --> 00:06:06,314
قَدْ مَنَّ اللَّهُ عَلَيْنَا

67
00:06:06,524 --> 00:06:09,169
Allah has indeed been gracious to us.

68
00:06:12,478 --> 00:06:15,716
I want you to pay attention to the following segments of the Ayah(آية).

69
00:06:17,263 --> 00:06:23,367
If you would forget everything that we said in the story of Yusuf(يوسُف); make sure that you don't forget this.

70
00:06:24,438 --> 00:06:26,889
Because this is the essence of the story of Yusuf(يوسُف).

71
00:06:29,262 --> 00:06:31,516
This is the essence of the story of Yusuf(يوسُف).

72
00:06:33,850 --> 00:06:38,407
And keep in mind that this story was revealed to Rasool Allah ﷺ when?

73
00:06:38,946 --> 00:06:40,780
When was Surah(سورة) Yusuf(يوسُف) revealed?

74
00:06:41,415 --> 00:06:41,915
In Makkah;

75
00:06:41,945 --> 00:06:42,777
When in Makkah?

76
00:06:43,459 --> 00:06:45,189
In the Aam Il Huzn(عام الهزن);

77
00:06:45,697 --> 00:06:49,180
In the Aam Il Huzn(عام الهزن); When Abu Talib(ابو طالب) passed away;

78
00:06:49,553 --> 00:06:52,142
and Khadijah رضي الله عنها  passed away;

79
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:58,162
and Rasool Allah ﷺ found no one to support him with strength like his Uncle Abu Talib(ابوطالب);

80
00:06:58,440 --> 00:07:02,440
and no one to support him financially like his wife Khadijah(خديجه),

81
00:07:02,956 --> 00:07:05,087
that was the year of sorrow.

82
00:07:05,262 --> 00:07:11,103
It's not only sorrow and sadness on Rasool Allah ﷺ because he lost his uncle and he lost his beloved wife.

83
00:07:11,421 --> 00:07:21,060
But because the Da'wah(دعوة) was limited and now barriers were being erected in the face of Rasool Allah ﷺ;

84
00:07:21,488 --> 00:07:24,879
before that Rasool Allah ﷺ had strength;

85
00:07:25,586 --> 00:07:32,640
His uncle was providing him with an umbrella and his wife was comforting him at home.

86
00:07:33,045 --> 00:07:36,362
Now Rasool Allah ﷺ has lost these two supporters

87
00:07:36,735 --> 00:07:41,481
and the heart of Rasool Allah ﷺ was filled with sadness and sorrow.

88
00:07:42,299 --> 00:07:45,751
Those moments that Rasool Allah ﷺ was going through are unbearable.

89
00:07:45,997 --> 00:07:48,896
So Rasool Allah ﷺ is receiving Surat Yusuf(سورة يوسُف);

90
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:52,959
In this particular situation because that is what Qur'an;

91
00:07:53,174 --> 00:07:54,753
لِنُثَبِّتَ بِهِ فُؤَادَكَ

92
00:07:55,007 --> 00:07:57,465
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى when he said will reveal in Quran; Why?

93
00:07:57,623 --> 00:07:59,242
لِنُثَبِّتَ بِهِ فُؤَادَكَ

94
00:07:59,495 --> 00:08:01,703
So that We would strengthen your heart.

95
00:08:02,655 --> 00:08:07,433
So Quran was being revealed on Rasool Allah ﷺ in the appropriate times;

96
00:08:07,949 --> 00:08:12,053
for the appropriate situations to serve the appropriate purpose.

97
00:08:13,822 --> 00:08:17,346
So in that specific period of Aam Il Huzn(عام الهزن);

98
00:08:17,695 --> 00:08:21,069
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى reveals to Rasool Allah ﷺ the story of Yusuf(يوسُف);

99
00:08:22,338 --> 00:08:30,041
it is the story of someone; who went through difficulty, trials, Misery, sorrow and sadness.

100
00:08:30,732 --> 00:08:32,089
But then in the end;

101
00:08:32,525 --> 00:08:33,763
قَدْ مَنَّ اللَّهُ عَلَيْنَا

102
00:08:33,793 --> 00:08:35,801
Allah has bestowed His blessing on me.

103
00:08:36,674 --> 00:08:37,603
Why?

104
00:08:38,349 --> 00:08:41,328
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says in this segment of the Ayah(آية);

105
00:08:41,662 --> 00:08:43,646
The essence of the Surah(سورة) of Yusuf(يوسُف);

106
00:08:43,844 --> 00:09:03,917
إِنَّهُ مَنْ يَتَّقِ وَيَصْبِرْ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يُضِيعُ أَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِينَ۝

107
00:09:04,375 --> 00:09:16,383
Verily, He who has Taqwa(تقوى) and is patient, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will not waste the deeds of  Al-Muhsineen(محسنين), the right doers.

108
00:09:17,534 --> 00:09:23,772
If you have Taqwa(تقوى) and patience; Eventually you will win; even after a while.

109
00:09:24,407 --> 00:09:30,596
If you have Taqwa(تقوى) and patience, no matter what, in the end, you will be victorious

110
00:09:30,771 --> 00:09:33,461
and you should have no doubt in that.

111
00:09:35,033 --> 00:09:39,400
SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) was victorious in the end; In Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and in Akhirah(آخرة).

112
00:09:39,599 --> 00:09:42,543
It's not only in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا); It's In Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and in Akhirah(آخرة).

113
00:09:43,408 --> 00:09:45,872
But it happened after a while it took a while.

114
00:09:45,962 --> 00:09:48,682
It wasn't swiftly in the same day; It took a while.

115
00:09:48,928 --> 00:09:50,460
Therefore, it needs patience.

116
00:09:50,516 --> 00:09:55,016
If you do not have patience, you will not be able to survive the long road.

117
00:09:55,918 --> 00:09:58,117
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is telling Rasool Allah ﷺ;

118
00:09:58,569 --> 00:10:01,210
There's a lot of struggling; There's a lot of striving;

119
00:10:01,583 --> 00:10:06,718
But if you have patience and you have Taqwa(تقوى), Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will establish you on the land.

120
00:10:07,067 --> 00:10:09,091
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says about Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل);

121
00:10:09,242 --> 00:10:15,385
وَجَعَلْنَا مِنْهُمْ أَئِمَّةً يَهْدُونَ بِأَمْرِنَا لَمَّا صَبَرُواْ ۖ وَكَانُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا يُوقِنُونَ۝

122
00:10:15,648 --> 00:10:20,445
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said; We have made the children of Israel(اسرائيل), Aimma(أئمَّة); leaders,

123
00:10:20,695 --> 00:10:23,156
leaders whom you follow in righteousness.

124
00:10:23,608 --> 00:10:25,197
أَئِمَّةً يَهْدُونَ بِأَمْرِنَا

125
00:10:25,257 --> 00:10:26,675
They guide to our path;

126
00:10:26,810 --> 00:10:27,603
When?

127
00:10:27,905 --> 00:10:30,746
When were the children of Israel(اسرائيل) leaders for mankind?

128
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:31,842
لَمَّا صَبَرُواْ ۖ

129
00:10:31,872 --> 00:10:32,857
When they had patience;

130
00:10:32,887 --> 00:10:34,493
وَكَانُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا يُوقِنُونَ۝

131
00:10:34,523 --> 00:10:35,442
And they had Yaqeen(يقين).

132
00:10:37,332 --> 00:10:39,240
There is no victory without Sabr(صبر).

133
00:10:40,454 --> 00:10:41,922
إنَّ نَصَر مع الصبر

134
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:45,576
It is mentioned in a Hadith(حديث); Victory comes with patience.

135
00:10:46,782 --> 00:10:54,427
And in general, today; We are very emotional.

136
00:10:54,855 --> 00:10:56,681
We are fired up fast.

137
00:10:58,268 --> 00:11:05,521
There could be a very hot Khutba(خطبه) of Jumu'ah(جُمعه) talking about Jihad(جهاد) for example.

138
00:11:06,981 --> 00:11:10,756
During that Khutba(خطبة) everyone feels that he is like Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

139
00:11:11,129 --> 00:11:12,677
He's ready to go in the battlefield.

140
00:11:13,471 --> 00:11:19,949
The Salah(صلاة) is over; a few moments just by the time you step your foot out of the Masjid(مسجد);

141
00:11:20,695 --> 00:11:25,100
You leave all of that emotions behind you, and you're back to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) again.

142
00:11:25,576 --> 00:11:30,131
Very easily fired up; and very easily we cool down.

143
00:11:31,464 --> 00:11:33,861
That is not Sabr(صبر); that is not Sabr(صبر).

144
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:35,649
We are reactionary.

145
00:11:35,871 --> 00:11:41,847
We act to situations; But then after a while, we'll calm down, and it's back to usual.

146
00:11:42,919 --> 00:11:47,942
But with Sahabah رضي الله عنهم; they had a plan.

147
00:11:48,109 --> 00:11:50,584
And they implemented that plan steadily.

148
00:11:51,910 --> 00:11:54,957
And they worked on it, and eventually they were victorious.

149
00:11:55,473 --> 00:12:02,582
Not only does this work with the believers, this is a law of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; that can even be applied to the Non-believer.

150
00:12:03,336 --> 00:12:07,775
Antara Bin Shaddad(أنترة بن شداد) is a famous figure in the Arab tales.

151
00:12:08,783 --> 00:12:14,901
As somebody who was very courageous, that's the personality of Antara(أنترة) in the Arabic literature.

152
00:12:15,107 --> 00:12:23,690
They say that Antara Bin Shaddad(أنترة بن شداد); A very strong well built powerful man came to him and said;

153
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:30,913
 Antara(أنترة), how come, you are famous as being powerful and strong when your body is smaller than mine;

154
00:12:31,262 --> 00:12:33,619
And your strength is less than my strength;

155
00:12:33,929 --> 00:12:38,201
Nevertheless, everyone uses you as the example of courage and strength.

156
00:12:38,518 --> 00:12:39,550
He said; I'll tell you why.?

157
00:12:40,368 --> 00:12:44,439
Stick your finger in my mouth and I'll stick my finger in your mouth and let's bite.

158
00:12:45,916 --> 00:12:48,012
I'll bite your finger and you bite mine.

159
00:12:48,631 --> 00:12:53,663
Both of them; they stick their fingers in each other's mouth, and they counted to three and they started biting

160
00:12:54,044 --> 00:12:56,925
and they're crushing on the fingers of each other.

161
00:12:58,377 --> 00:13:03,701
After a few moments; the other guy screamed, and he lost.

162
00:13:04,574 --> 00:13:06,207
Antara(أنترة) told him: That's why.?

163
00:13:07,183 --> 00:13:13,226
If you would have just waited for one more moment, one more second, I would have screamed.

164
00:13:16,511 --> 00:13:19,836
It's just a matter of outdoing you;

165
00:13:20,526 --> 00:13:24,177
I was able to have patience for just one more moment and that's why I won.

166
00:13:25,574 --> 00:13:27,806
As I say in English; Who blinks first,

167
00:13:28,837 --> 00:13:32,964
إِنَّهُ مَنْ يَتَّقِ وَيَصْبِرْ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يُضِيعُ أَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِينَ۝

168
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:52,113
قَالُواْ تَٱللَّهِ لَقَدۡ ءَاثَرَكَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡنَا وَإِن كُنَّا لَخَٰطِـِٔينَ۝

169
00:13:52,402 --> 00:13:55,408
Now they realize their loss and they said;

170
00:13:55,678 --> 00:13:59,821
By Allah; Indeed Allah has preferred you above us and we certainly have been sinners.

171
00:13:59,955 --> 00:14:04,095
These brothers who were jealous of Yusuf(يوسُف), so jealous they tried to kill him.

172
00:14:04,277 --> 00:14:05,809
Now they're saying you're better than us.

173
00:14:06,436 --> 00:14:08,523
You are better than us; In the end they had to admit it.

174
00:14:08,793 --> 00:14:11,839
See how Allah made him victorious in every aspect.

175
00:14:12,704 --> 00:14:15,950
They even reach to the level where his brothers said; You are better than us; Now we admit.

176
00:14:16,045 --> 00:14:36,141
قَالَ لَا تَثۡرِيبَ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡيَوۡمَۖ يَغۡفِرُ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡۖ وَهُوَ أَرۡحَمُ ٱلرَّـٰحِمِينَ۝

177
00:14:36,512 --> 00:14:41,133
When Rasool Allah ﷺ went into Makkah.

178
00:14:42,339 --> 00:14:45,093
He went into Makkah victorious without any parades;

179
00:14:45,210 --> 00:14:46,689
without any national anthem;

180
00:14:46,749 --> 00:14:48,034
without any red carpet;

181
00:14:48,152 --> 00:14:49,429
without any motorcade;

182
00:14:49,557 --> 00:14:50,664
without any pride;

183
00:14:50,933 --> 00:14:58,626
Rasool Allah ﷺ instead of riding on his horse or camel with his chest forward, carrying his spear.

184
00:14:58,880 --> 00:15:05,237
Rasool Allah ﷺ went into Makkah, making Sujood(سجود) to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى on his camel;

185
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:08,948
Until his beard was touching the back of the camel;

186
00:15:09,472 --> 00:15:13,980
Tawadhua(تواضع) humbleness with Sakeena(سكينة) calmness.

187
00:15:14,535 --> 00:15:19,781
Until he reached to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), and he climbed on the door of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه);

188
00:15:20,035 --> 00:15:21,988
while the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are surrounding him.

189
00:15:22,234 --> 00:15:31,211
His enemy for years and years are now under the sword of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

190
00:15:31,545 --> 00:15:33,864
So Rasool Allah ﷺ asked them; What Do you think I will do with you?

191
00:15:34,011 --> 00:15:35,050
They said;

192
00:15:35,614 --> 00:15:37,201
أَخٌ كَرِيمٌ، وَابْنُ أَخٍ كَرِيمٍ،

193
00:15:37,704 --> 00:15:40,439
A noble brother and the son of a noble brother.

194
00:15:42,494 --> 00:15:45,005
Today I will tell you, like what Yusuf(يوسُف) told his brother;

195
00:15:45,035 --> 00:15:46,541
لَا تَثۡرِيبَ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡيَوۡمَۖ

196
00:15:47,859 --> 00:15:51,999
I'm gonna tell you just what Yusuf(يوسُف) told his brother;

197
00:15:52,301 --> 00:15:56,269
Today; there's no punishment or no blame on you.

198
00:15:56,650 --> 00:15:58,032
اذهبوا فأنتم الطلقاء

199
00:15:58,400 --> 00:15:59,686
Go; You are free.

200
00:16:01,860 --> 00:16:05,456
He said; No reproach on you this day; May Allah forgive you;

201
00:16:05,694 --> 00:16:08,195
And He is the Most Merciful of those who showed mercy.

202
00:16:08,338 --> 00:16:10,767
So he forgave his brothers, and he allowed them to leave.

203
00:16:11,322 --> 00:16:12,481
But he gave them something.

204
00:16:13,045 --> 00:16:15,329
And this is a miracle of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

205
00:16:15,519 --> 00:16:17,250
He gave them his shirt.

206
00:16:18,138 --> 00:16:22,887
And he said; Throw it on my father, and he will see;

207
00:16:23,379 --> 00:16:24,673
Because his father was blind.

208
00:16:24,824 --> 00:16:27,298
Why was he blind, crying on SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف).

209
00:16:27,328 --> 00:16:30,028
And this is a miracle of SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف).

210
00:16:30,512 --> 00:16:55,560
ٱذۡهَبُواْ بِقَمِيصِي هَٰذَا فَأَلۡقُوهُ عَلَىٰ وَجۡهِ أَبِي يَأۡتِ بَصِيرٗا وَأۡتُونِي بِأَهۡلِكُمۡ أَجۡمَعِينَ۝

211
00:16:56,133 --> 00:16:59,593
Go with this shirt of mine and cast it over the face of my father;

212
00:16:59,884 --> 00:17:04,273
He will become clear sighted and bring to me all your family.

213
00:17:06,591 --> 00:17:08,764
When the caravan was leaving out of Egypt;

214
00:17:10,748 --> 00:17:15,836
Yaqoob(يعقوب) was in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) very far away a few hundred miles away;

215
00:17:16,121 --> 00:17:18,826
When the caravan just started moving out of Egypt;

216
00:17:19,326 --> 00:17:21,882
Syedina(سيدنا) Yaqoob(يعقوب) smelled SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف).

217
00:17:22,334 --> 00:17:23,858
He was smelling his shirt.

218
00:17:25,151 --> 00:17:29,017
And it was still in Egypt and this is another miracle of Syedina Yaqoob عليه السّلام.

219
00:17:29,231 --> 00:17:54,286
وَلَمَّا فَصَلَتِ ٱلۡعِيرُ قَالَ أَبُوهُمۡ إِنِّي لَأَجِدُ رِيحَ يُوسُفَۖ لَوۡلَآ أَن تُفَنِّدُونِ۝

220
00:17:54,654 --> 00:18:00,103
And when the caravan departed, their father said; I do indeed feel the smell of Yusuf(يوسُف);

221
00:18:00,471 --> 00:18:02,931
If only you think me not a dotard;

222
00:18:03,019 --> 00:18:05,678
A person who has weakness of mind because of old age.

223
00:18:07,257 --> 00:18:09,250
They said;

224
00:18:09,377 --> 00:18:22,066
قَالُواْ تَٱللَّهِ إِنَّكَ لَفِي ضَلَٰلِكَ ٱلۡقَدِيمِ۝

225
00:18:22,532 --> 00:18:26,435
This is something that one of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) of Qur'an said;

226
00:18:26,465 --> 00:18:28,015
لقد قال الذي كلمة العظيمة

227
00:18:28,045 --> 00:18:30,753
They have said something inappropriate to their father.

228
00:18:31,166 --> 00:18:32,729
They said oh our father;

229
00:18:33,110 --> 00:18:36,210
By Allah certainly you are in your old error.

230
00:18:36,503 --> 00:18:39,480
They told him; You had became old; You're starting to lose your mind.

231
00:18:40,622 --> 00:19:00,689
فَلَمَّآ أَن جَآءَ ٱلۡبَشِيرُ أَلۡقَىٰهُ عَلَىٰ وَجۡهِهِۦ فَٱرۡتَدَّ بَصِيرٗاۖ

232
00:19:01,522 --> 00:19:18,976
قَالَ أَلَمۡ أَقُل لَّكُمۡ إِنِّيٓ أَعۡلَمُ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ۝

233
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:25,587
Then when the bearer of the glad tidings arrived, he cast it over his face and he became clear sighted;

234
00:19:25,617 --> 00:19:30,396
He said; Did I not say to you I know from Allah that which you know not.

235
00:19:30,642 --> 00:19:32,913
And now they realize their mistake again they said;

236
00:19:33,001 --> 00:19:53,914
قَالُواْ يَـٰٓأَبَانَا ٱسۡتَغۡفِرۡ لَنَا ذُنُوبَنَآ إِنَّا كُنَّا خَٰطِـِٔينَ۝

237
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:59,841
O; our father asked for forgiveness from Allah for our sins; Indeed we have been sinners.

238
00:20:00,103 --> 00:20:18,540
قَالَ سَوۡفَ أَسۡتَغۡفِرُ لَكُمۡ رَبِّيٓۖ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلۡغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ۝

239
00:20:19,008 --> 00:20:22,169
He said; I will ask my Lord for forgiveness for you.

240
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:27,026
Verily He only is the One, Who's oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.

241
00:20:27,915 --> 00:20:36,786
Now all of them moved, they took their belongings, everything with them and they started moving towards Egypt.

242
00:20:37,971 --> 00:20:41,423
To fulfill the invitation of SadyinaYusuf عليه السّلام.

243
00:20:41,820 --> 00:20:48,966
As soon as they came in, SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) has prepared to meet his family.

244
00:20:49,212 --> 00:21:16,321
فَلَمَّا دَخَلُواْ عَلَىٰ يُوسُفَ ءَاوَىٰٓ إِلَيۡهِ أَبَوَيۡهِ وَقَالَ ٱدۡخُلُواْ مِصۡرَ إِن شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ ءَامِنِينَ۝

245
00:21:16,612 --> 00:21:20,315
Then when they entered onto Yusuf(يوسُف), he took his parents to himself and said;

246
00:21:20,529 --> 00:21:23,569
Enter Egypt if Allah will; in security.

247
00:21:24,553 --> 00:21:28,532
And he had the throne; SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) was sitting on a high throne.

248
00:21:29,135 --> 00:21:33,556
So he elevated his father and his mother to sit with him on the throne.

249
00:21:33,944 --> 00:21:41,749
And then all of them the father and the mother, and the 11 brothers made Sujood(سجود) to SadyinaYusuf عليه السّلام;

250
00:21:41,964 --> 00:21:44,782
To fulfill the dream, which he saw when he was a child.

251
00:21:45,481 --> 00:21:50,703
So the end of the Surah(سورة) of Yusuf(يوسُف) fulfills the dream, which was in the beginning of the Surah(سورة) of Yusuf(يوسُف)

252
00:21:50,830 --> 00:21:57,957
between them; very long lifespan, the scholars have given it 30 years, some of them 25, some of them 80 years;

253
00:21:58,029 --> 00:21:58,719
 Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم).

254
00:21:59,156 --> 00:22:02,574
This is the fulfillment of the dream of SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف).

255
00:22:02,653 --> 00:22:31,525
إِذۡ قَالَ يُوسُفُ لِأَبِيهِ يَـٰٓأَبَتِ إِنِّي رَأَيۡتُ أَحَدَ عَشَرَ كَوۡكَبٗا وَٱلشَّمۡسَ وَٱلۡقَمَرَ رَأَيۡتُهُمۡ لِي سَٰجِدِينَ۝

256
00:22:32,075 --> 00:22:35,812
I see 11 planets making Sujood(سجود) to me and the sun and the moon.

257
00:22:36,202 --> 00:22:42,019
So these 11 planets were his brothers, and the sun is his father and the moon is his mother.

258
00:22:43,789 --> 00:23:03,028
وَقَالَ يَـٰٓأَبَتِ هَٰذَا تَأۡوِيلُ رُءۡيَٰيَ مِن قَبۡلُ قَدۡ جَعَلَهَا رَبِّي حَقّٗاۖ

259
00:23:03,803 --> 00:23:11,014
O my father; This is the interpretation of my dream of old, my Lord has made it come true.

260
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:13,094
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

261
00:23:13,832 --> 00:23:43,858
وَقَدۡ أَحۡسَنَ بِيٓ إِذۡ أَخۡرَجَنِي مِنَ ٱلسِّجۡنِ وَجَآءَ بِكُم مِّنَ ٱلۡبَدۡوِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ أَن نَّزَغَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ بَيۡنِي وَبَيۡنَ إِخۡوَتِيٓۚ

262
00:23:44,285 --> 00:23:47,342
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; These are the words of Yusuf(يوسُف);

263
00:23:47,930 --> 00:23:49,443
He was indeed good to me;

264
00:23:50,451 --> 00:23:52,447
When He took me out of the prison,

265
00:23:52,858 --> 00:23:55,437
and brought me here out of the bedouin life;

266
00:23:55,787 --> 00:23:59,166
After Satan has sown enmity between me and my brothers;

267
00:23:59,368 --> 00:24:03,836
Certainly in my Lord is the Most courteous and kind unto whom He will.

268
00:24:04,010 --> 00:24:07,719
Truly He only He is the All Knowing, the All Wise.

269
00:24:08,726 --> 00:24:27,476
رَبِّ قَدۡ ءَاتَيۡتَنِي مِنَ ٱلۡمُلۡكِ وَعَلَّمۡتَنِي مِن تَأۡوِيلِ ٱلۡأَحَادِيثِۚ

270
00:24:29,171 --> 00:24:57,611
فَاطِرَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ أَنتَ وَلِيِّۦ فِي ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۖ تَوَفَّنِي مُسۡلِمٗا وَأَلۡحِقۡنِي بِٱلصَّـٰلِحِينَ۝

271
00:24:57,964 --> 00:25:04,607
My Lord, you have indeed bestowed on me the sovereignty, and taught me the interpretation of dreams,

272
00:25:04,805 --> 00:25:06,726
the only Creator of the heavens and the earth;

273
00:25:06,972 --> 00:25:10,210
You are my Wali(ولي) in this world and the hereafter.

274
00:25:10,496 --> 00:25:15,758
SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) had everything a seeker of this world wants.

275
00:25:17,441 --> 00:25:22,948
I mean; No matter how hard we work, you can't get anything better than what Yusuf(يوسُف) had;

276
00:25:23,012 --> 00:25:25,679
In terms of the standards of this world.

277
00:25:26,281 --> 00:25:28,409
He had power and authority.

278
00:25:29,044 --> 00:25:35,465
He was combined with his parents and family again, and the dispute among them was solved.

279
00:25:36,322 --> 00:25:37,338
He had wealth.

280
00:25:37,957 --> 00:25:43,607
He had control over the kingdom of Egypt, which was the greatest kingdom of the time.

281
00:25:43,909 --> 00:25:45,036
He had it all.

282
00:25:47,528 --> 00:25:53,456
If somebody had; what Yousuf عليه السّلام had; He would hold it, with his teeth and nails.

283
00:25:54,313 --> 00:25:55,599
And not want to leave it.

284
00:25:56,409 --> 00:26:02,571
You remember; When Suleman Ibn Malik(سليمان إبن عبدالملك) asked Abu Hazim(أبوحازم); Why do we hate death?

285
00:26:03,095 --> 00:26:06,095
What did Abu Hazim(أبوحازم) say? He said;

286
00:26:06,658 --> 00:26:12,041
عمرتم دنياكم وخربتم آخرتكم فتكرهون ان تخرجومن العمران الى الخراب

287
00:26:12,367 --> 00:26:15,736
He said; You have built this world and you have destroyed Aakhirah(آخِرة).

288
00:26:15,903 --> 00:26:18,839
So you hate to go from what is built, to what is destroyed.

289
00:26:20,896 --> 00:26:25,298
SadyinaYusuf عليه السّلام had everything that a person would want in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

290
00:26:26,028 --> 00:26:28,258
But this for SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) is nothing.

291
00:26:29,552 --> 00:26:31,932
He's not a seeker of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

292
00:26:33,565 --> 00:26:36,811
He would say; Alhamdulillah(ألحمدلله) for what Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given me;

293
00:26:37,263 --> 00:26:40,446
but he's doing it as a Ibadah(عبادة) for Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

294
00:26:41,954 --> 00:26:52,155
So Yusuf(يوسُف) when he is in the pinnacle and the peak of his power and fame and wealth and dominance on the face of the earth;

295
00:26:52,313 --> 00:26:54,084
Look at the Dua(دُعَا) of SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف).

296
00:26:54,727 --> 00:26:58,076
Look at the Dua(دُعَا), that SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) is saying; He said;

297
00:26:58,274 --> 00:27:11,181
تَوَفَّنِي مُسۡلِمٗا وَأَلۡحِقۡنِي بِٱلصَّـٰلِحِينَ۝

298
00:27:11,702 --> 00:27:18,828
SadyinaYusuf عليه السّلام said; Cause me to die as a Muslim and join me with the righteous.

299
00:27:19,630 --> 00:27:24,892
You have Kingdom; you have power; you have fame; you have wealth; you have love in the hearts of everyone;

300
00:27:25,384 --> 00:27:27,559
Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) in his eyes is nothing.

301
00:27:29,361 --> 00:27:30,322
Subhan Allah Hil Azeem(سُبْحان الله العظيم)

302
00:27:30,352 --> 00:27:33,638
and we have a few dollars and we're clinging to it;

303
00:27:33,964 --> 00:27:38,892
And we're afraid of death; for Mataa Qalil(متاع قليل);

304
00:27:39,796 --> 00:27:42,995
Mataa An-Zail(متاع زائل) for something that is going to leave.

305
00:27:45,122 --> 00:27:46,439
And we're holding tight to it.

306
00:27:46,884 --> 00:27:48,937
SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) has all of this and he is saying;

307
00:27:49,167 --> 00:27:51,287
تَوَفَّنِي مُسۡلِمٗا وَأَلۡحِقۡنِي بِٱلصَّـٰلِحِينَ۝

308
00:27:52,297 --> 00:27:55,461
Make me die as a Muslim and be with the righteous.

309
00:27:56,814 --> 00:27:59,996
These are the hearts who were attached to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and attached to Aakhirah(آخِرة).

310
00:28:00,227 --> 00:28:01,385
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

311
00:28:01,584 --> 00:28:29,595
ذَٰلِكَ مِنۡ أَنۢبَآءِ ٱلۡغَيۡبِ نُوحِيهِ إِلَيۡكَۖ وَمَا كُنتَ لَدَيۡهِمۡ إِذۡ أَجۡمَعُوٓاْ أَمۡرَهُمۡ وَهُمۡ يَمۡكُرُونَ۝

312
00:28:29,882 --> 00:28:35,738
This is of the news of the unseen, which we reveal by inspiration to you;

313
00:28:35,913 --> 00:28:42,081
you were not present with them; when they raised their plan together and also while they were plotting.

314
00:28:42,327 --> 00:28:55,802
وَمَآ أَكۡثَرُ ٱلنَّاسِ وَلَوۡ حَرَصۡتَ بِمُؤۡمِنِينَ۝

315
00:28:56,008 --> 00:29:00,452
And most of mankind will not believe even if you desire, eagerly.

316
00:29:01,452 --> 00:29:07,202
We'll start now with a story of a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

317
00:29:07,710 --> 00:29:09,900
who was not mentioned in reference to Da'wah(دعوة).

318
00:29:12,440 --> 00:29:17,356
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى when He talked about Noah(نوح), it was the Da'wah(دعوة) of Noah(نوح).

319
00:29:18,221 --> 00:29:21,102
When He talked about Hood(هود); it was the Da'wah(دعوة) of Hood(هود).

320
00:29:21,181 --> 00:29:22,762
Salih(صالح); it was the Da'wah(دعوة) of Salih(صالح).

321
00:29:22,873 --> 00:29:24,333
Noah(نوح); it was the Da'wah(دعوة) of Noah(نوح).

322
00:29:24,587 --> 00:29:29,722
But with this particular Nabi(نَبِي); Allahسُبحانه وتعالى did not talk about his Da'wah(دعوة) at all.

323
00:29:31,595 --> 00:29:33,659
Syedina Ayub عليه السّلام.

324
00:29:34,678 --> 00:29:37,218
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; when he talked about Syedina Ayub(سيدنا ايوب);

325
00:29:38,059 --> 00:29:40,321
He did not mention his Da'wah(دعوة) to his people.

326
00:29:41,416 --> 00:29:45,321
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى mentioned the story of his Sabr(صبر), his patience.

327
00:29:47,360 --> 00:29:52,132
And that alone deserved his story to be mentioned twice and Qur'an;

328
00:29:53,117 --> 00:30:02,533
In reference of his patience, so it became later proverb; Sabr Ayub(صبرايوب).

329
00:30:03,724 --> 00:30:07,160
Whenever we want to describe patience, we say patience of Ayub(أيوب);

330
00:30:07,644 --> 00:30:10,277
He became the symbol of Sabr(صبر); patience.

331
00:30:10,491 --> 00:30:12,055
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

332
00:30:12,491 --> 00:30:28,965
وَٱذْكُرْ عَبْدَنَآ أَيُّوبَ إِذْ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُۥٓ أَنِّى مَسَّنِىَ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ بِنُصْبٍۢ وَعَذَابٍ۝

333
00:30:29,285 --> 00:30:35,196
And remember Our slave; Job; when he invoked his Lord saying;

334
00:30:35,226 --> 00:30:40,208
Verily, Satan has touched me with distress and torment.

335
00:30:40,859 --> 00:30:44,212
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says in Surat Al-Ambiyaa(سورة الأنبِيَاء).

336
00:30:44,668 --> 00:30:55,445
وَأَيُّوبَ إِذْ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُ أَنِّي مَسَّنِيَ الضُّرُّ وَأَنتَ أَرْحَمُ الرَّاحِمِينَ۝

337
00:30:55,576 --> 00:30:58,334
And remember Ayub(أيوب); when he cried to his Lord;

338
00:30:58,479 --> 00:31:04,005
Verily distress has seized me and you are the Most Merciful of those who show mercy.

339
00:31:05,529 --> 00:31:10,836
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) says that Syedina Ayub عليه السلام was very wealthy

340
00:31:12,391 --> 00:31:17,415
and he had a large family and he was very healthy and strong.

341
00:31:19,460 --> 00:31:22,738
So he had health, wealth and family.

342
00:31:25,222 --> 00:31:37,106
And then suddenly; Syedina Ayub عليه السّلام lost his family somehow; lost his wealth and he lost his health.

343
00:31:39,447 --> 00:31:45,834
And this did not happen; gradually; It happened suddenly. He lost everything.

344
00:31:46,985 --> 00:31:52,306
He lost everything that a person loves in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

345
00:31:53,147 --> 00:31:55,433
المال والبنون زينة الحياة الدنيا

346
00:31:55,464 --> 00:32:00,165
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; Children and wealth are the adornment of this life.

347
00:32:00,658 --> 00:32:05,158
Whether you are Muslim or non Muslim, this is something that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has put the love in your heart;

348
00:32:05,411 --> 00:32:07,279
 Your wealth and your family.

349
00:32:07,398 --> 00:32:12,286
It's something that we love in this world, and that is the Zeenah(زينة); that is the adornment of this world.

350
00:32:12,540 --> 00:32:15,309
 Ayub(أيوب) lost these two and in addition to that, he lost his health

351
00:32:15,468 --> 00:32:19,094
and his health situation became so bad;

352
00:32:21,011 --> 00:32:25,592
that he was not able to move, he was not able to work

353
00:32:26,291 --> 00:32:34,406
and then the particular type of disease that he had was a disease that the people used to view in a form of Tashaum(تشاعم);

354
00:32:34,477 --> 00:32:40,527
they used to have a bad omen or evil Omen from this and they used to despise that particular disease.

355
00:32:40,803 --> 00:32:44,631
And anybody who's inflicted with it, they will stay away from him.

356
00:32:45,044 --> 00:32:47,323
So he became an outcast in the society.

357
00:32:47,569 --> 00:32:50,942
And it is said that they even forced him out of the village;

358
00:32:51,109 --> 00:32:53,823
So he was living outside of his town.

359
00:32:55,778 --> 00:32:57,453
He had no source of income.

360
00:32:58,913 --> 00:33:01,365
So it is said that his wife started to work.

361
00:33:03,281 --> 00:33:06,662
She would cook for people serve them in their homes,

362
00:33:07,043 --> 00:33:13,679
but then the people did not want to interact with her because they were afraid that she could also infect them.

363
00:33:14,409 --> 00:33:16,282
 So nobody wants to hire her.

364
00:33:17,258 --> 00:33:20,147
So the situation of Syedina Ayub(سيِّدنا أيوب) was deteriorating.

365
00:33:20,528 --> 00:33:25,440
And this was over a span of years; It was not a matter of a few weeks or months.

366
00:33:27,861 --> 00:33:33,312
And it said that even the close ones around him his wife and his brothers and his family were saying;

367
00:33:34,535 --> 00:33:39,183
If Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has any love for him, this wouldn't have happened to him.

368
00:33:40,564 --> 00:33:42,969
That was difficult for Syedina Ayub(سيِّدنا أيوب) to hear

369
00:33:43,245 --> 00:33:46,809
and that is when Syedina Ayub(سيِّدنا أيوب) made his Dua(دُعَا) to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and said;

370
00:33:47,102 --> 00:33:50,964
Harm has inflicted me and you are the Most Merciful.

371
00:33:51,433 --> 00:33:53,107
And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

372
00:33:53,137 --> 00:33:54,409
فَاسْتَجَبْنَا لَهُ

373
00:33:54,766 --> 00:33:56,917
We responded to his Dua(دُعَا).

374
00:33:58,036 --> 00:34:01,858
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى accepted the Dua(دُعَا) of Syedina Ayub عليه السّلام.

375
00:34:03,208 --> 00:34:04,281
How did it happen?

376
00:34:04,636 --> 00:34:06,298
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told him;

377
00:34:06,668 --> 00:34:16,353
ارْكُضْ بِرِجْلِكَ ۖ هَٰذَا مُغْتَسَلٌ بَارِدٌ وَشَرَابٌ۝

378
00:34:16,671 --> 00:34:23,599
Strike the ground with your foot; This is a spring of water to wash in cool and refreshing to drink.

379
00:34:24,597 --> 00:34:27,819
So he was commanded to hit the ground with his foot.

380
00:34:28,351 --> 00:34:29,850
So water came out;

381
00:34:30,334 --> 00:34:34,909
He was ordered by Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to wash his body with that water;

382
00:34:35,163 --> 00:34:40,584
So it would heal him and purify him from the outside and to drink it and it will heal him from the inside.

383
00:34:41,822 --> 00:34:47,006
So that replace the health of Syedina Ayub(سيِّدنا أيوب).

384
00:34:47,858 --> 00:34:49,065
And the Ayah(آية) says;

385
00:34:49,295 --> 00:35:03,974
وَوَهَبْنَا لَهُ أَهْلَهُ وَمِثْلَهُم مَّعَهُمْ رَحْمَةً مِّنَّا وَذِكْرَىٰ لِأُولِي الْأَلْبَابِ۝

386
00:35:04,207 --> 00:35:10,549
And We have given him a replacement of his family like them and better; Mercy from Us.

387
00:35:10,819 --> 00:35:13,167
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gave him back his family,

388
00:35:13,197 --> 00:35:17,324
whether it was reviving the dead or providing him with new members of family; Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم);

389
00:35:17,490 --> 00:35:20,881
But he had equal to what he had before and even better.

390
00:35:22,175 --> 00:35:24,540
So now his family was replaced.

391
00:35:25,167 --> 00:35:26,334
What about his wealth?

392
00:35:26,627 --> 00:35:29,725
We find that in a Hadith(حديث) narrated by Bukhari(بخاريْ);

393
00:35:29,854 --> 00:35:31,394
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

394
00:35:31,577 --> 00:35:35,664
When Ayub(أيوب) was taking a shower naked;

395
00:35:35,958 --> 00:35:42,535
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى sent on him grasshoppers made of gold that were falling over him.

396
00:35:43,131 --> 00:35:46,313
Syedina Ayub(سيِّدنا أيوب) was gathering them and collecting them.

397
00:35:46,504 --> 00:35:48,242
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Ayub(أيوب);

398
00:35:48,948 --> 00:35:53,046
Isn't it Me; Who will provide for you; So why are you gathering all of this?

399
00:35:53,234 --> 00:35:56,377
He said; O Allah, this is Your mercy and I want to have more of it.

400
00:35:57,298 --> 00:36:01,034
It's a miracle Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provided him with grasshoppers made of gold;

401
00:36:02,121 --> 00:36:07,507
As a reward for the patience of His servant Ayub عليه السّلام.

402
00:36:07,856 --> 00:36:09,395
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

403
00:36:10,221 --> 00:36:14,030
وَوَهَبْنَا لَهُ أَهْلَهُ وَمِثْلَهُم مَّعَهُمْ رَحْمَةً مِّنَّا

404
00:36:14,380 --> 00:36:16,842
And in another Ayah(آية) Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

405
00:36:16,977 --> 00:36:24,882
وَآتَيْنَاهُ أَهْلَهُ وَمِثْلَهُم مَّعَهُمْ رَحْمَةً مِّنْ عِندِنَا

406
00:36:25,287 --> 00:36:31,320
رَحْمَةً مِّنْ عِندِنَا وَذِكْرَىٰ لِلْعَابِدِينَ۝

407
00:36:31,368 --> 00:36:32,849
Notice this; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

408
00:36:32,879 --> 00:36:38,030
So we answered his call, we removed his distress and we restored his family to him

409
00:36:38,189 --> 00:36:43,414
and the like there off along with them as a mercy from Ourselves

410
00:36:43,652 --> 00:36:45,144
and a reminder for who?

411
00:36:45,676 --> 00:36:47,295
وَذِكْرَىٰ لِلْعَابِدِينَ۝

412
00:36:47,906 --> 00:36:49,914
The story of Ayub(أيوب); Allah is saying

413
00:36:50,176 --> 00:36:54,903
that it is a reminder for Al-Aabideen(ألعابدين); the worshipers of Allah.

414
00:36:55,673 --> 00:37:03,837
Notice the word Al-Aabideen(ألعابدين), when you are worshiping Allahسُبحانه وتعالى you need to have a lot of patience.

415
00:37:05,504 --> 00:37:10,524
Because worshipping Allahسُبحانه وتعالى needs commitment and discipline and persistence.

416
00:37:11,119 --> 00:37:23,336
This is very easy to suddenly go into an emotional outburst and pray and read Qur'an and follow the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

417
00:37:23,955 --> 00:37:29,628
It's very easy to do that; Sometimes we find that people crash into the religion and they start practicing;

418
00:37:30,961 --> 00:37:34,350
but it's not easy to persist and continue with it.

419
00:37:37,646 --> 00:37:40,465
And that is why Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

420
00:37:40,525 --> 00:37:41,727
شَيَّبَتْنِي هودٌ

421
00:37:42,790 --> 00:37:46,617
Hud(هود) has made my hair turn gray.

422
00:37:47,578 --> 00:37:51,244
What is the Ayah(آية) in Syedina Hud(سيدنا هود) Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

423
00:37:51,506 --> 00:37:54,252
فَاسْتَقِمْ كَمَا أُمِرْتَ

424
00:37:54,828 --> 00:37:57,137
Stay on the straight path.

425
00:37:58,161 --> 00:38:02,534
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is telling Muhammadﷺ to stick on the straight path for all of your life.

426
00:38:03,461 --> 00:38:08,247
And that is Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying; It made my hair turned gray

427
00:38:08,453 --> 00:38:12,888
because it is easy to worship Allahسُبحانه وتعالى for a few days and night

428
00:38:12,993 --> 00:38:16,318
but to discipline yourself to do it continuously it needs patience.

429
00:38:17,009 --> 00:38:19,406
To pray Witr(وتر) continuously; it need patience;

430
00:38:19,454 --> 00:38:23,549
to fast; it needs patience; to pray in Jama'ah(جماعة) it needs patience;

431
00:38:23,605 --> 00:38:25,961
to make Zikr(ذكر) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى it needs patience;

432
00:38:26,174 --> 00:38:33,714
that's why Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has closed the Ayah(آية) of the story of Ayub(أيوب) with this final comment,

433
00:38:33,897 --> 00:38:35,158
وَذِكْرَىٰ لِلْعَابِدِينَ۝

434
00:38:35,182 --> 00:38:38,333
It's a reminder for those, who are worshipping Allah.

435
00:38:39,357 --> 00:38:44,703
And this is a form of Bala(بلى); This is a form of testing that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى puts on the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

436
00:38:45,195 --> 00:38:46,909
 Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

437
00:38:48,314 --> 00:38:53,534
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى tests the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) with the most severe tests.

438
00:38:54,066 --> 00:38:55,280
And then As-Saliheen(الصالحين);

439
00:38:55,415 --> 00:38:56,562
فالأمثل فالأمثل

440
00:38:56,592 --> 00:38:58,631
And then the best of you.

441
00:39:00,122 --> 00:39:02,979
The more strong you are and firm in your Deen(دِيْن);

442
00:39:03,170 --> 00:39:06,860
the more difficult the test of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى on you; will be.

443
00:39:07,618 --> 00:39:08,856
Just like in school;

444
00:39:09,840 --> 00:39:13,737
The professors when they write tests, or the teachers when they write test,

445
00:39:14,309 --> 00:39:16,813
they write a group of easy questions,

446
00:39:16,964 --> 00:39:18,512
the average difficulty questions

447
00:39:18,718 --> 00:39:26,100
and then they put a few tough questions here and there to separate between the high segment of the class.

448
00:39:26,386 --> 00:39:30,323
So you have a group of questions which are easy those will be answered by the majority.

449
00:39:30,673 --> 00:39:34,125
And then you have another group of questions that will be answered by a lesser group.

450
00:39:34,292 --> 00:39:38,124
And that is separate between, the D and the C.

451
00:39:38,323 --> 00:39:41,212
And then you have questions that will separate between the B and the C.

452
00:39:41,481 --> 00:39:44,839
And then you have questions that will separate between the A and the B.

453
00:39:44,966 --> 00:39:49,099
And then you have one or two questions that will separate between the A Plus and the A Minus.

454
00:39:50,877 --> 00:39:54,715
So, everyone is receiving questions according to his level.

455
00:39:55,025 --> 00:39:56,906
And that is to put them through this ranking;

456
00:39:56,936 --> 00:40:02,476
If you made all of the questions easy, everyone will get 100% the full score and everyone will pass.

457
00:40:02,714 --> 00:40:09,666
So you have to put the questions in a gradual step by step level of difficulty to separate between these students.

458
00:40:09,737 --> 00:40:13,277
The same thing with the test that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى puts on us in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

459
00:40:13,436 --> 00:40:17,557
If your Eeman(ايمان)  is weak, Allah will give you a simple exam.

460
00:40:17,961 --> 00:40:23,430
If your level of Eeman(ايمان) is strong, then you would receive a more difficult exam.

461
00:40:23,588 --> 00:40:27,498
And these tests that the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى go through are more severe.

462
00:40:27,664 --> 00:40:33,601
Not only, are they severe in their tests and Da'wah(دعوة), even in their illness it's more difficult.

463
00:40:33,990 --> 00:40:38,493
Abdullah Ibn Masood(عبدالله ابن مسعود) was visiting Rasool Allah ﷺ his death; illness.

464
00:40:39,429 --> 00:40:44,025
So Abdullah Ibn Masood(عبدالله ابن مسعود) put his hand over Rasool Allah ﷺ; temperature was so high.

465
00:40:44,191 --> 00:40:45,266
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

466
00:40:45,398 --> 00:40:48,283
نعم إني أُوعَك كما يوعك رجلان منك

467
00:40:48,736 --> 00:40:54,014
Rasool Ullah said; I go through fever that two of you would go through.

468
00:40:54,791 --> 00:40:57,022
The fever on Rasool Allah ﷺ was double.

469
00:40:57,701 --> 00:40:58,090
Why?

470
00:40:58,120 --> 00:41:03,863
Because of the level of Rasool Allah ﷺ he had to go through more difficult tests from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

471
00:41:04,435 --> 00:41:11,568
The next story is the story of Zan-Noon(ذا النون); Sahib Al-Hoot(صاحب الحوت); Syedina Yunus عليه السّلام.

472
00:41:12,187 --> 00:41:14,274
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has called him; Zan-Noon(ذا النون)

473
00:41:14,449 --> 00:41:17,838
and Noon(نون) is the big fish or whale;

474
00:41:18,147 --> 00:41:19,900
Sahib Al-Hoot(صاحب الحوت) is the same thing.

475
00:41:20,440 --> 00:41:21,535
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

476
00:41:21,565 --> 00:41:23,829
وَإِنَّ يُونُسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ۝

477
00:41:24,108 --> 00:41:27,351
And verily Jonah was one of His messengers.

478
00:41:29,034 --> 00:41:33,034
Syedina Yunus عليه السّلام was sent to a town in Iraq.

479
00:41:34,867 --> 00:41:38,218
He made Da'wah(دعوة) to his people calling them to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

480
00:41:38,248 --> 00:41:40,035
As usual, they did not respond.

481
00:41:40,551 --> 00:41:42,535
And they were harsh on him;

482
00:41:43,654 --> 00:41:49,056
Syedina Yunus(سيدنا يونس) was irritated by their response and agitated.

483
00:41:51,111 --> 00:41:57,270
His people provoked him because of their persistence and animosity towards the religion of Allah.

484
00:41:58,302 --> 00:41:59,397
Syedina Yunus(سيدنا يونس) said;

485
00:41:59,427 --> 00:42:04,627
If this is the situation with these people, they don't deserve this, I will leave and I'll go somewhere else.

486
00:42:04,754 --> 00:42:07,894
I'll go and make Da'wah(دعوة) in other parts of the world, I will leave these people alone.

487
00:42:07,954 --> 00:42:10,092
They don't deserve this; Look at their response.

488
00:42:10,584 --> 00:42:12,608
وَذَا النُّونِ إِذ ذَّهَبَ مُغَاضِبًا

489
00:42:12,872 --> 00:42:15,702
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; And Zan-Noon(ذا النون), he left angry;

490
00:42:16,321 --> 00:42:18,750
He left his people in a state of anger.

491
00:42:19,170 --> 00:42:21,567
They did not respond; They don't want to listen;

492
00:42:21,694 --> 00:42:23,361
I'm going to leave and go somewhere else.

493
00:42:24,745 --> 00:42:28,674
So he left them, and he wants to get as far as possible; So he went in the sea.

494
00:42:29,166 --> 00:42:34,879
And he took a boat to go in the sea; so it take him as far as possible from these people; who he despised.

495
00:42:36,269 --> 00:42:41,503
Wind picked up, waves were getting higher and higher; It was a storm.

496
00:42:42,496 --> 00:42:47,710
The people were in that boat, they decided that in order for us to survive, we have to get rid of our luggage.

497
00:42:47,740 --> 00:42:51,667
 They threw all of their luggage; to make the book lighter.

498
00:42:52,239 --> 00:42:53,413
That wasn't enough.

499
00:42:53,620 --> 00:42:58,647
So now they have to throw in; one of the passengers.

500
00:42:58,916 --> 00:43:03,583
They have to throw out; one of the passengers; they have to sacrifice one of the men onboard.

501
00:43:04,337 --> 00:43:08,186
So they cast lots like what we say today; throw a dice.

502
00:43:09,201 --> 00:43:13,789
So they cast the lot it came on who; Yunus(يونس).

503
00:43:14,567 --> 00:43:19,681
They said; No, No, No. We're not gonna get rid of Yunus(يونس); This is our Barakah(بركة); This is our blessing on the boat.

504
00:43:19,923 --> 00:43:23,085
He's the best man; we have on board; We're not going to get rid of him.

505
00:43:23,998 --> 00:43:26,279
Let's try again; They throw it another time.

506
00:43:26,361 --> 00:43:27,365
It came on who?

507
00:43:27,710 --> 00:43:28,158
Yunus(يونس);

508
00:43:28,218 --> 00:43:31,403
Another time; They did it a third time; it came on Yunus(يونس).

509
00:43:31,433 --> 00:43:33,384
And these people; they didn't want to get rid of Yunus(يونس).

510
00:43:33,971 --> 00:43:36,261
They saw how righteous he was; They don't want to get rid of him.

511
00:43:36,439 --> 00:43:39,291
Syedina Yunus(يونس) knew that this is not random.

512
00:43:40,146 --> 00:43:42,127
These casting of the lots is not random;

513
00:43:42,157 --> 00:43:44,953
This is by the will of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and Allah is telling him something.

514
00:43:45,882 --> 00:43:48,236
So he jumped in the sea.

515
00:43:48,432 --> 00:43:54,345
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى commanded one of His creation; the whale or the big fish to swallow him.

516
00:43:54,924 --> 00:43:56,902
So it swallowed Syedina Yunus(سيدنا يونس).

517
00:43:57,633 --> 00:44:01,719
They say; the Mufasireen(مفسرين); some of the commentators on Qur'an; they say

518
00:44:02,283 --> 00:44:05,368
that Yunus(يونس) was unconscious.

519
00:44:07,788 --> 00:44:13,969
And then he woke up in the stomach of Al-Hoot(ألحوت); the whale.

520
00:44:15,731 --> 00:44:19,119
And he looked around him, and he thought that he is where?

521
00:44:19,278 --> 00:44:20,127
In the grave.

522
00:44:20,778 --> 00:44:23,832
He thought he's dead; for a while;

523
00:44:24,329 --> 00:44:26,289
but that impression did not last long.

524
00:44:26,797 --> 00:44:35,058
Because he started touching around him and he found out that this is not a grave, this is the stomach of a whale.

525
00:44:37,336 --> 00:44:44,066
Now obviously, a stomach of a whale is not a five star hotel, it's not a comfortable place to be.

526
00:44:44,613 --> 00:44:46,820
Stomach of whale is intended to do what?

527
00:44:47,026 --> 00:44:48,407
To digest food.

528
00:44:50,060 --> 00:44:57,859
And some of the most powerful enzymes and digesting fluids are in the stomachs of fish.

529
00:44:59,197 --> 00:45:03,706
Because if you notice fish do not chew their food; they swallow it whole.

530
00:45:04,294 --> 00:45:08,770
If you dissect the stomach of a fish, you would find the whole fish in there;

531
00:45:09,294 --> 00:45:17,753
And they have disintegrated and melted because of the power of the enzymes; It just breaks apart the flesh.

532
00:45:19,976 --> 00:45:30,204
So Syedina Yunus(سيدنا يونس), his flesh, his skin was peeling off; his flesh his skin was falling out.

533
00:45:31,569 --> 00:45:36,971
The stomach did not know this is Syedina Yunus(سيدنا يونس); a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allah; it was digesting him just like any other meal.

534
00:45:37,677 --> 00:45:39,701
 So his skin was peeling out.

535
00:45:40,882 --> 00:45:46,974
Syedina Yunus عليه السّلام in this moment of difficulty, he ran to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; And he made Sujood(سجود)

536
00:45:48,394 --> 00:45:49,742
and he told Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

537
00:45:49,772 --> 00:45:55,265
O Allah I am making Sujood(سجود) to you in a place; where no one made Sujood(سجود) to you before; in the stomach of whale.

538
00:45:55,725 --> 00:45:59,923
And then he made his famous Dua(دُعَا) which was recorded in Qur'an.

539
00:46:00,396 --> 00:46:00,871
He said;

540
00:46:00,931 --> 00:46:11,075
فَنَادَىٰ فِي الظُّلُمَاتِ أَن لَّا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا أَنتَ سُبْحَانَكَ

541
00:46:11,250 --> 00:46:17,114
 سُبْحَانَكَ إِنِّي كُنتُ مِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ۝

542
00:46:17,177 --> 00:46:18,723
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

543
00:46:19,027 --> 00:46:20,469
فَنَادَىٰ فِي الظُّلُمَاتِ

544
00:46:21,170 --> 00:46:23,416
And he called in the darkness.

545
00:46:24,003 --> 00:46:24,805
He said;

546
00:46:25,019 --> 00:46:30,115
None has the right to be worshipped but You glorified and exalted be You;

547
00:46:30,464 --> 00:46:32,739
Truly I have been of the wrongdoers.

548
00:46:32,972 --> 00:46:39,127
An admission of guilt, and witness of the oneness of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

549
00:46:39,524 --> 00:46:40,682
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

550
00:46:40,712 --> 00:46:42,143
فَنَادَىٰ فِي الظُّلُمَاتِ

551
00:46:42,596 --> 00:46:45,231
He cried in the darkness.

552
00:46:46,071 --> 00:46:48,908
This was the darkness of the stomach of the whale;

553
00:46:49,567 --> 00:46:54,544
In the darkness of the sea; In the darkness of the night; three darknesses.

554
00:46:56,766 --> 00:46:58,766
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

555
00:47:00,179 --> 00:47:08,159
The angels see Hilkah Az-Zikr(حلقه الذكر) the meetings of remembrance of Allah; like stars,

556
00:47:09,262 --> 00:47:10,737
which you see in the sky.

557
00:47:11,796 --> 00:47:13,838
We use the stars to navigate;

558
00:47:14,791 --> 00:47:19,901
The angels use these stars on earth to know where Allah is being remembered.

559
00:47:20,885 --> 00:47:24,846
Whenever a group of Muslims come together, and we hope to be one of those.

560
00:47:26,084 --> 00:47:29,747
This appears to the creation of the heavens; Like a star,

561
00:47:30,700 --> 00:47:32,888
and they see it and they come to it,

562
00:47:33,346 --> 00:47:38,657
so that they can witness the circles of remembering Allah and make Dua(دُعَا) for the ones; who are in it.

563
00:47:38,935 --> 00:47:43,294
So we ask Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to surround us with the angels of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى

564
00:47:43,324 --> 00:47:46,554
and to accept their Dua(دُعَا) and to make us of those who are forgiven.

565
00:47:47,564 --> 00:47:50,208
So even though this was in the depths of the ocean;

566
00:47:50,873 --> 00:47:54,101
In the middle of the stomach of the whale; in the darkness of the night;

567
00:47:54,578 --> 00:48:03,593
the weak voice of Syedina Yunus(سيدنا يونس) was heard by the angels in the utmost heavens.

568
00:48:05,299 --> 00:48:10,053
These angels went to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and said; O Allah;

569
00:48:10,733 --> 00:48:13,670
اليس هذا الصوت عبدك صالح فلان

570
00:48:14,025 --> 00:48:17,258
Isn't this the sound of your righteous servant?

571
00:48:18,057 --> 00:48:21,342
الذي ما ذال يصعد له العمل الصالح في اليل والنهار

572
00:48:21,446 --> 00:48:27,245
Isn't this the sound of your righteous servant whom used to do good night and day?

573
00:48:27,911 --> 00:48:28,910
يصعد له العمل الصالح

574
00:48:28,934 --> 00:48:35,373
They used to say; We would see his good deeds going up in the sky in the night and in the day.

575
00:48:36,024 --> 00:48:38,579
So this sound was familiar to them.

576
00:48:38,730 --> 00:48:40,127
They knew who he was.

577
00:48:40,157 --> 00:48:40,746
Why?

578
00:48:40,889 --> 00:48:45,056
Because they would see pillars of light going up in the sky

579
00:48:45,198 --> 00:48:48,563
because of his good deeds that he used to do every day and every night.

580
00:48:48,929 --> 00:48:52,010
They knew; who he was; This sound was familiar to them.

581
00:48:52,891 --> 00:48:53,889
They knew him;

582
00:48:54,817 --> 00:49:01,552
because the good deeds are like pillars of light that traveling in the sky and reach to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and passed by the angels.

583
00:49:01,954 --> 00:49:05,144
They said; O Allah; Aren't you gonna have mercy on him?

584
00:49:05,803 --> 00:49:07,573
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said; Yes.

585
00:49:07,795 --> 00:49:11,666
And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى tells us in Qur'an, the reason why?

586
00:49:12,253 --> 00:49:23,652
فَلَوْلَا أَنَّهُ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُسَبِّحِينَ ۝ لَلَبِثَ فِي بَطْنِهِ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ۝

587
00:49:24,015 --> 00:49:25,358
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

588
00:49:25,517 --> 00:49:30,018
If it was not for the fact that he used to remember Us before;

589
00:49:30,351 --> 00:49:34,026
he would have remained in the stomach of the whale; until the day of judgment.

590
00:49:35,526 --> 00:49:40,487
Because he remembered Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in moments of ease;

591
00:49:40,788 --> 00:49:43,567
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى took care of him in moments of difficulty.

592
00:49:43,867 --> 00:49:44,947
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

593
00:49:44,977 --> 00:49:47,143
تعرف على الله في الرخاء يعرفك في الشدة

594
00:49:47,342 --> 00:49:52,062
Remember Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in moments of ease, Allah will remember you in moments of difficulty.

595
00:49:53,235 --> 00:49:55,727
We need to remember Allah in our young age;

596
00:49:55,854 --> 00:49:57,799
So that Allah will remember us in our old age.

597
00:49:58,037 --> 00:50:01,634
Remember Allah; when you're healthy, so Allah remember you when you are ill;

598
00:50:01,808 --> 00:50:05,737
Remember Allah when you have free time; So Allah will remember you, when you become busy.

599
00:50:05,895 --> 00:50:11,627
Remember Allahسُبحانه وتعالى  when you are alive, so Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will remember you; when you're dead.

600
00:50:12,826 --> 00:50:18,036
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى took care of Syedina Yunus(سيدنا يونس) in the depths of the darkness of the sea

601
00:50:18,233 --> 00:50:19,568
because of this Dua(دُعَا).

602
00:50:19,782 --> 00:50:21,774
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى freed him;

603
00:50:22,092 --> 00:50:23,465
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

604
00:50:23,525 --> 00:50:28,668
فَاستَجَبنا لَهُ وَنَجَّيناهُ مِنَ الغَمِ

605
00:50:28,756 --> 00:50:32,668
So we answered his call and delivered him from the distress.

606
00:50:33,779 --> 00:50:36,390
One of the companions came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

607
00:50:36,564 --> 00:50:41,207
Is this Dua(دُعَا) only applicable to Syedina Yunus(سيدنا يونس)?

608
00:50:41,493 --> 00:50:43,337
Or would it apply to any one of us?

609
00:50:43,608 --> 00:50:46,743
Meaning Can we make the use of the same Dua(دُعَا) and it will be accepted?

610
00:50:47,076 --> 00:50:50,686
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Yes; didn't you see Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said;

611
00:50:50,870 --> 00:50:54,856
وَكَذَٰلِكَ نُنجِي الْمُؤْمِنِينَ۝

612
00:50:54,994 --> 00:50:56,953
And thus we saved the believers.

613
00:50:57,975 --> 00:51:01,840
Because Allah says; We saved Yunus(يونس) and thus we save the believers.

614
00:51:02,046 --> 00:51:03,700
Therefore Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

615
00:51:03,730 --> 00:51:04,655
هذا دعا الكرب

616
00:51:04,871 --> 00:51:07,483
This is the Dua(دُعَا) of the distress.

617
00:51:08,238 --> 00:51:11,785
If you ask Allahسُبحانه وتعالى using this Dua(دُعَا);

618
00:51:11,845 --> 00:51:14,301
Allah will deliver you from your distress.

619
00:51:14,460 --> 00:51:15,581
The Dua(دُعَا) again is;

620
00:51:15,817 --> 00:51:19,625
لَّا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا أَنتَ سُبْحَانَكَ إِنِّي كُنتُ مِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ۝

621
00:51:23,180 --> 00:51:26,539
Yunus(يونس) was delivered out of the stomach of the whale

622
00:51:27,039 --> 00:51:30,444
and he was delivered to safety on the shore.

623
00:51:31,262 --> 00:51:34,220
But he did not have skin to protect him from the sunrays;

624
00:51:34,601 --> 00:51:36,966
He did not have skin to protect him from wind.

625
00:51:38,347 --> 00:51:41,831
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى delivered him to the shore;

626
00:51:42,069 --> 00:51:48,355
And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى commanded a tree to go grow over Syedina Yunus(سيدنا يونس);

627
00:51:48,561 --> 00:51:53,053
so that it would provide cover and shade for him and it will also provide him with food.

628
00:51:53,267 --> 00:51:54,357
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

629
00:51:54,513 --> 00:52:00,697
وَأَنبَتْنَا عَلَيْهِ شَجَرَةً مِّن يَقْطِينٍ۝

630
00:52:00,804 --> 00:52:04,269
Allah planted over him a tree of Yaqteen(يقطين).

631
00:52:04,975 --> 00:52:07,264
But now Yunus(يونس) has to finish his job.

632
00:52:07,987 --> 00:52:10,262
So last time, come back to his town; Go back.

633
00:52:11,248 --> 00:52:12,700
So he went back to his people.

634
00:52:13,033 --> 00:52:23,232
وَأَرْسَلْنَاهُ إِلَىٰ مِائَةِ أَلْفٍ أَوْ يَزِيدُونَ ۝ فَآمَنُوا فَمَتَّعْنَاهُمْ إِلَىٰ حِينٍ۝

635
00:52:23,401 --> 00:52:28,743
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; We sent him to 100,000 people or even more.

636
00:52:29,274 --> 00:52:30,039
What happened?

637
00:52:30,330 --> 00:52:31,407
فَآمَنُوا

638
00:52:31,473 --> 00:52:33,094
They believed in him?

639
00:52:33,759 --> 00:52:35,163
All of them accepted Islam.

640
00:52:36,789 --> 00:52:38,497
فَمَتَّعْنَاهُمْ إِلَىٰ حِينٍ۝

641
00:52:38,557 --> 00:52:40,980
So we gave them enjoyment for a while.

642
00:52:41,623 --> 00:52:46,709
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says that the people of Yunus(يونس) are an exception.

643
00:52:48,844 --> 00:52:55,333
Because before the other nations of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) were being destroyed.

644
00:52:56,634 --> 00:53:00,984
But with the people of Yunus عليه السّلام; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

645
00:53:01,603 --> 00:53:05,151
فَلَوْلَا كَانَتْ قَرْيَةٌ آمَنَتْ فَنَفَعَهَا إِيمَانُهَا

646
00:53:05,254 --> 00:53:11,900
 إِلَّا قَوْمَ يُونُسَ لَمَّا آمَنُوا كَشَفْنَا عَنْهُمْ عَذَابَ الْخِزْيِ فِي الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا وَمَتَّعْنَاهُمْ إِلَىٰ حِينٍ۝

647
00:53:12,210 --> 00:53:19,032
Was there any town that believed after seeing the punishment and its faith saved it from the punishment?

648
00:53:19,266 --> 00:53:23,550
The answer is; None except the people of Yunus(يونس) when they believed;

649
00:53:23,622 --> 00:53:30,410
We removed from them the torment and disgrace in their life and we gave them enjoyment in this world for a while.

650
00:53:30,695 --> 00:53:34,997
It is said that when Yunus(يونس) left the punishment was hovering over them.

651
00:53:35,965 --> 00:53:38,345
That's it; I mean the punishment was about to strike.

652
00:53:39,044 --> 00:53:42,647
But because Yunus(يونس) left immaturely.

653
00:53:43,266 --> 00:53:48,061
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى held away that punishment, and then when Yunus(يونس) came, they responded,

654
00:53:48,320 --> 00:53:52,439
and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى saved them from a punishment that was already hovering over their heads.

655
00:53:56,746 --> 00:54:04,830
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in Surat Al-Qalam(سورة ألقلم) tells Rasool Allah ﷺ about this story.

656
00:54:06,409 --> 00:54:08,838
And this was revealed in the period in Makkah.

657
00:54:10,711 --> 00:54:16,076
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was receiving the same response of the people of Yunus(يونس); Rejection.

658
00:54:18,528 --> 00:54:25,172
So to keep Rasool Allah ﷺ from doing the same thing that Yunus(يونس) did.

659
00:54:25,545 --> 00:54:29,432
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Muhammadﷺ about the story of Yunus(يونس)

660
00:54:29,861 --> 00:54:35,067
and the first word that was used before the narration of the story is; Fasbir(فصبر).

661
00:54:35,777 --> 00:54:36,769
Have Patience.

662
00:54:37,019 --> 00:54:48,066
فَاصْبِرْ لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ وَلَا تَكُن كَصَاحِبِ الْحُوتِ إِذْ نَادَىٰ وَهُوَ مَكْظُومٌ۝

663
00:54:48,582 --> 00:55:02,357
لَّوْلَا أَن تَدَارَكَهُ نِعْمَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِ لَنُبِذَ بِالْعَرَاءِ وَهُوَ مَذْمُومٌ۝

664
00:55:02,976 --> 00:55:09,497
فَاجْتَبَاهُ رَبُّهُ فَجَعَلَهُ مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ۝

665
00:55:09,715 --> 00:55:10,942
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

666
00:55:11,092 --> 00:55:14,069
So wait with patience for the decision of your Lord;

667
00:55:14,315 --> 00:55:19,735
and be not like the Companion of the fish; When he cried out to us while he was in deep sorrow;

668
00:55:19,934 --> 00:55:26,068
Had not the grace from his Lord reached him; He would indeed have been left in the stomach of the fish.

669
00:55:26,298 --> 00:55:30,916
So he was cast off on the naked shore; while he was to be blamed;

670
00:55:31,138 --> 00:55:35,051
but his Lord chose him and made him of the righteous.

671
00:55:35,456 --> 00:55:38,752
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى chose him and made him of the righteous.

672
00:55:39,871 --> 00:55:42,657
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

